# Custom Column Components

`ComponentType.CUSTOM` lets you render anything you like for a column. The component receives `{ key, value, item, colProps }` so it can format the cell value, look up related fields on the row, or even render interactive controls.

Pair it with `formatValue` for cheap formatting (locale-aware currencies, dates) where you don't need a full component.

```typescript
import type { CustomComponentTypeProperties } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable/dataComponent';
import AvatarCell from './AvatarCell.svelte';
import ProgressCell from './ProgressCell.svelte';
import ActionsCell from './ActionsCell.svelte';

const config: DataTableConfig<Project> = {
	type: 'projects',
	columnProperties: {
		owner: {
			type: ComponentType.CUSTOM,
			sortable: false,
			component: AvatarCell
		} satisfies CustomComponentTypeProperties<Project['owner']>,

		progress: {
			type: ComponentType.CUSTOM,
			sortable: true,
			component: ProgressCell
		} satisfies CustomComponentTypeProperties<number>,

		budget: {
			type: ComponentType.NUMBER,
			formatValue: (value) =>
				new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, {
					style: 'currency',
					currency: 'USD',
					maximumFractionDigits: 0
				}).format(value as number)
		},

		actions: {
			type: ComponentType.CUSTOM,
			sortable: false,
			component: ActionsCell
		} satisfies CustomComponentTypeProperties<unknown>
	},
	dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id'
};
```

A custom cell that mounts an action button should call `event.stopPropagation()` in its handlers so clicks don't bubble up and toggle the row's modal:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import type { CustomComponentProps } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable/dataComponent';
	import type { Project } from './projectData.js';

	let { item }: CustomComponentProps<unknown, Project> = $props();

	function archive(event: MouseEvent) {
		event.stopPropagation();
		// ...
	}
</script>

<button onclick={archive}>Archive</button>
```

